WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.417
This is one page of a water filter manual.

2
00:00:03.417 --> 00:00:05.690
Now, watch the same steps.

3
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.828
Put a tray below.

4
00:00:07.828 --> 00:00:09.565
Close the cold water valve.

5
00:00:09.565 --> 00:00:12.303
Then open the filter faucet until the water stops.

6
00:00:12.953 --> 00:00:15.680
Fit the wrench around the first canister.

7
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.622
Seen from below, turn it counterclockwise.

8
00:00:18.622 --> 00:00:20.197
Lower it straight down.

9
00:00:20.846 --> 00:00:23.543
Empty it, and take out the old cartridge.

10
00:00:23.543 --> 00:00:27.458
Check that the O-ring is clean, and flat in its groove.

11
00:00:28.108 --> 00:00:30.474
Remove the plastic wrap.

12
00:00:30.474 --> 00:00:33.007
Stage one is the sediment cartridge.

13
00:00:33.007 --> 00:00:34.935
Center it on the knob at the bottom.

14
00:00:35.585 --> 00:00:38.481
Stage two is granular carbon.

15
00:00:38.481 --> 00:00:40.652
The rubber washer goes up.

16
00:00:40.652 --> 00:00:42.687
Stage three is the carbon block.

17
00:00:43.336 --> 00:00:45.651
Turn each canister clockwise by hand,

18
00:00:45.651 --> 00:00:47.388
until it stops.

19
00:00:47.388 --> 00:00:51.006
Then, only a quarter to a half turn more with the wrench.

20
00:00:51.656 --> 00:00:54.913
Open the valve slowly, and look for leaks.

21
00:00:54.913 --> 00:00:57.509
Let the faucet run until the water is clear.

22
00:00:58.209 --> 00:01:01.945
Right order, dry cabinet, and no call to support.
